      "writtenOn": "2024-02-21T08:30:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can understand using the Duration is recommend by the API guidline now. But setTtlDuration(null) means use default Duration is confusing...\n\nShall we consider the following two API?\n\n```\nsetTtlDuration(@NonNull Duration ttlDuration)\n\nsetDefaultTtlDuration()\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 222,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 222,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "b9dcc4302d2608df08e12d855a085c2606c2b0f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e8ca1030_c92021cc",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/nsd/AdvertisingRequest.java",
        "patchSetId": 89
      },
      "lineNbr": 222,
      "author": {
        "id": 1693933
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-21T08:39:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e But setTtlDuration(null) means use default Duration is confusing...\n\nThis is equivalent to that the user never calls `setTltDuration()`, which is the default behavior of existing service registration APIs.\n\nWhen the custom TTL duration is not set, the default behavior is that SRV, TXT and A/AAAA will use different TTL values, so it\u0027s probably not easy to use a non-null TTL duration to represent the default behavior. Using a `@Nullable Duration mTltDuration;` is straight forward, and it is generally suggested by the API guideline that @nullable properties should access @nullable arugment in the setter (to keep symmetric with the getter): see go/android-api-guidelines#builders-optional-nullable-setters",
      "parentUuid": "a48eca1e_23bde784",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 222,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 222,
        "endChar": 35
      },
